      "id": "mk_slope_e_001",
      "question": "Find the equation of the line passing through (2, 3) and (-1, 6).",
      "choices": {
        "A": "y = x + 1",
        "B": "y = -x + 5",
        "C": "y = 2x - 1",
        "D": "y = -2x + 7",
        "E": "y = 3x"
      },
      "answer": "B",
      "explanation": "Slope: m = (6 - 3) / (-1 - 2) = 3 / (-3) = -1. Using point-slope form with (2, 3): y - 3 = -1(x - 2) ⇒ y - 3 = -x + 2 ⇒ y = -x + 5.",
      "steps": [
        "1. Find slope: m = (y₂ - y₁) / (x₂ - x₁) = (6 - 3) / (-1 - 2) = -1.",
        "2. Use point-slope: y - y₁ = m(x - x₁).",
        "3. y - 3 = -1(x - 2).",
        "4. y - 3 = -x + 2.",
        "5. y = -x + 5."
      ],
      "fastStrategy": "Find slope; use point-slope form; convert to slope-intercept."
    }
  ]
